## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/cameraimport.html
- Summary (EN): Creates a zero layer positioned to match a chosen camera's view, so other nodes can use it as a reference; typically used with Match Camera COP or Rasterize Geometry COP. Output named camera_ref. Listed as available since 22.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud cameraimport crée une couche placée dans l'espace d'une caméra existante, pour servir de référence à d'autres nœuds.

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Signature", "meaning": "Layer type accepted by the source; see the Signatures section of the glossary"}, {"name": "Camera", "meaning": "Object camera whose view the layer matches, using the camera path syntax"}, {"name": "Near", "meaning": "Near clipping plane, used only when enabled"}, {"name": "Far", "meaning": "Far clipping plane, used only when enabled"}]

